00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:09,480
This, he said, contained the essential principle of animalism.

2
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:15,239
Whoever had thoroughly grasped it would be safe from human influences."

3
00:00:15,239 --> 00:00:21,920
The birds at first objected, since it seemed to them that they also had two legs.

4
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:26,000
But Snowball proved to them that this was not so.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
>> "A bird's wing, comrades, is an organ of propulsion and not of manipulation.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,239
It should therefore be regarded as a leg.

7
00:00:35,239 --> 00:00:42,039
The distinguishing mark of man is the hand, the instrument with which he does all his mischief."

8
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:47,840
>> The birds did not understand Snowball's long words, but they accepted his explanation,

9
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:54,840
and all the humbler animals set to work to learn the new maxim by heart.

10
00:00:54,840 --> 00:01:00,599
Four legs good, two legs bad, was inscribed on the end wall of the

11
00:01:00,599 --> 00:01:06,039
barn above the Seven Commandments and in bigger letters.

12
00:01:06,039 --> 00:01:10,639
When they had once got it by heart, the sheep developed a great liking for this

13
00:01:10,639 --> 00:01:16,280
maxim, and often, as they lay in the field, they would all start bleating:

14
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:21,400
>> "Four legs good, two legs bad! Four legs good, two legs bad!"

15
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:26,199
>> And keep it up for hours on end, never growing tired of it.

16
00:01:26,199 --> 00:01:30,920
Napoleon took no interest in Snowball's committees. He said that the education

17
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:34,719
of the young was more important than anything that could be done for those

18
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:37,119
who were already grown up.

19
00:01:37,119 --> 00:01:42,039
It happened that Jessie and Bluebell had both whelped soon after the hay harvest,

20
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:46,400
giving birth between them to nine sturdy puppies.

21
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:50,159
As soon as they were weaned, Napoleon took them away from their mothers,

22
00:01:50,159 --> 00:01:54,320
saying that he would make himself responsible for their education.

23
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:58,159
He took them up into a loft which could only be reached by a ladder from the

24
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:03,000
harness room, and there kept them in such seclusion that the rest of the farm
